# WOLF — Screening & Strategies

## One strategy definition

- Predefined, manual, and AI-built screeners share the same `StrategyDefinition` + ConditionRegistry.
- Gemini/LLM may emit structured strategy JSON only — never executable scanner code.
- Predefined screeners must work without AI.

## Screener output

Prefer structured results (adapt to existing types):

- symbol, matched, score, timestamps, metrics
- triggeredConditions / failedConditions
- explanation derived from real metrics — not vague “strong opportunity”

## Scoring

- WOLF SCORE = setup quality, never “% probability of profit”.
- Never hardcode `0` scores when engines produced data; do not fabricate scores.

## Radar UX

- Screener = WHAT; Universe = WHERE (no duplicate MARKET picker).
- User must know what/where/timeframe/conditions before and after scan.
- Stream matches while scanning full universe; display limits ≠ scan limits.

## WOLF Opportunities (12 defaults)

Independent: Momentum Burst, Breakout/Breakdown Radar, Long/Short Build-Up, Short Covering, Long Unwinding, Contraction→Breakout, Volume Anomaly, RS Leaders, Reversal Radar.  
**Confluence** combines them — multi-signal agreement, not double-counted indicator spam.

## UI

- Keep existing black/gold WOLF desk language; dense, professional, scannable.
- Do not redesign unrelated screens.
